answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "coincide with each other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fbfcf52-a469-59d1-919e-121969a6bbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "coincide with each other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567794} :answer-field/id #uuid "b15edfb4-b08c-555f-993b-677323b16295" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92749e76-b792-5359-a3ac-3281324e5da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "inconsistent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567802} {:answer/id #uuid "a14354ee-51e8-58d1-a086-585d69c607a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "consistent independent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567806} {:answer/id #uuid "bc04411c-e087-5c18-a43b-7d0ac7b290d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "consistent dependent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc04411c-e087-5c18-a43b-7d0ac7b290d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "consistent dependent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567811} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3d8da81-73c0-56a4-894d-d7ed736b31a5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d3d4bb5-4ee4-593d-9277-86ca83447b36" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 - 4x \\\\ y &=-4x + 1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nThe lines corresponding to the equations {{field-1}}. Therefore, the system has {{field-2}}, meaning that it's {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "A system of equations is *consistent* if it has at least one solution. Otherwise, it is called *inconsistent*.\n\nConsistent systems, in turn, can be of the following two types:\n\n- When a system of equations has a *single* solution, it is called *consistent independent*.\n- When a system of equations has an *infinite number* of solutions, it is called *consistent dependent*.\n\nWe can summarize these definitions using the diagram shown below.\n\n![](images/16/1692fbea298339ff839cf2f14986d51af45d1ec72b2b7d0de179336bdef40c0e.png)\n\nThe solutions of a linear system with two variables correspond to the points of intersection of the two lines defined by the equations. Three possibilities exist, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8c/8c544df38ce82dd70c3d01718233c9fae1fae0534748892643a12b6556918fb7.png)\n\nNotice that the equations in the system have the same slopes ($-4$) and the same $y$-intercepts ($1$). So, the lines $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{coincide with each other}}$ and share every point.\n\nTherefore, the system has $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{infinitely many solutions}}$, meaning that it's $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{consistent dependent}}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198347 :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Slope-Intercept Systems Using Consistency and Dependency Terminology"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459ee4e7-d316-5b20-8afd-8c68854b13de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567781} {:answer/id #uuid "539fe890-8821-50f4-818f-f915e1bf646e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "coincide with each other" :db/id #edb/ref 