ear system with two variables correspond to the points of intersection of the two lines defined by the equations. Three possibilities exist, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8c/8c544df38ce82dd70c3d01718233c9fae1fae0534748892643a12b6556918fb7.png)\n\nNotice that the equations in the system have distinct slopes ($7$ and $8$, respectively). So, the lines $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{intersect at one point}}$.\n\nTherefore, the system has $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{only one solution}}$, meaning that it's $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{consistent independent}}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198347 :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Slope-Intercept Systems Using Consistency and Dependency Terminology"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa24829-9dc3-5199-9dc2-a9135be578e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "consistent dependent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567776} {:answer/id #uuid "7a32a402-3890-5a79-af56-674c8f2d43ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "consistent independent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567798} {:answer/id #uuid "9f729bec-b424-5847-afa8-ff9e29ca7147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "inconsistent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f729bec-b424-5847-afa8-ff9e29ca7147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "inconsistent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567805} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c8a4f68-40e1-5679-8203-b1bc26fa4397" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff0ff22-f425-504b-b783-91f161ddfb0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860